        "--prompt-en",
        "Create an editorial fashion photograph in which a person is visible on the passenger deck of a ferry just after it leaves the harbor. The same supplied portrait guides the person's visible face and dark, straight hair with a soft fringe. The person pauses mid-turn toward the receding pier, shoulders and hips turning together in an easy three-quarter view; the glance connects the person to the crossing without turning the moment into a formal pose. The thoughtfully layered outfit keeps clean lines and one muted accent. A light deck breeze stirs the outer cloth as the turn settles, leaving the layered outline clear. clothing remains the image's clear visual focus. A generous full-length frame keeps the person's visible face, hair, and layered outline readable while showing both shoe soles resting flat on the same ferry deck, the person's weight balanced over both feet, and deck around the shoes; the receding pier and open shoreline remain legible behind. Overcast skylight creates broad, gentle transitions across the person's face, clothing, and ferry surfaces, leaving the flat sole-to-deck contacts readable; a narrow warm cabin reflection crosses the windbreak glass and echoes the profile. A small almost-smile keeps the photograph observed and composed, poised between leaving and arriving.",
